<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-theme="dark" data-accent="mint"><head>{% include "head.njk" %}<title>Professional profile — Ahmed Almadhoun</title><meta name="description" content="A concise, print-friendly professional profile of Ahmed Almadhoun: transport engineering, doctoral research, publications and analytical experience."><link rel="canonical" href="https://ahmedalmadhoun.com/profile/"></head><body><main class="section shell profile"><div class="profile-hero"><a class="text-link" href="/">← Back to website</a><h1>Ahmed Almadhoun<span class="accent-text">.</span></h1><p class="profile-subtitle">Transport engineer · Doctoral researcher · Analytical professional</p><p>Warsaw, Poland · Warsaw University of Technology, Faculty of Transport</p><div class="profile-actions"><button class="button button-primary" type="button" data-print hidden>Print / save as PDF ↗</button><a class="button button-quiet" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ahmed-madhoun/">LinkedIn ↗</a><a class="button button-quiet" href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=lB2_-wEAAAAJ&amp;hl=en">Google Scholar ↗</a></div></div><p>I investigate how transport networks shape freight accessibility and economic connectivity. My background combines civil engineering, transport modelling, doctoral research, university teaching and finance operations.</p><div class="profile-columns"><section><h2>Research & methods</h2><p>Doctoral research: transport poverty in freight transportation networks, under Prof. Mariusz Kostrzewski at Warsaw University of Technology.</p><ul><li>Freight accessibility and infrastructure constraints.</li><li>Passenger–freight interactions in shared urban corridors.</li><li>PTV Vissim microsimulation and PTV Visum network modelling.</li><li>Candidate indicators, calibration and empirical validation in development.</li></ul><h2>Professional experience</h2><p><strong>Warsaw University of Technology:</strong> doctoral research and teaching experience in engineering graphics and descriptive geometry.</p><p><strong>Accenture:</strong> accounts receivable and cash collections experience, reporting, escalations, month-end support and colleague training.</p><p><strong>Engineering foundation:</strong> civil engineering studies and master’s work modelling Wrocław’s transport system with PTV Visum.</p><h2>Recognition & direction</h2><p>2026 WUT scientific competition recognition and an awarded 2026–2027 grant on passenger-induced freight penalties under mixed-traffic conditions.</p><p>Next: expand corridor models and datasets, validate measures and integrate the doctoral contribution. Dissertation submission targeted for September 2028.</p></section><section><h2>Selected published research</h2><ul>{% for work in portfolio.works %}{% if work.status == 'Published' %}<li><strong>{{ work.title }}</strong><br>{{ work.venue }} · {{ work.year }}</li>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</ul><h2>Conference contributions</h2><p>TRANSCOM 2025 · Transport XXI Wieku 2025 · LSTP 2026 · TRANSBALTICA 2026.</p><h2>Presented & forthcoming</h2><ul><li><strong>TRANSBALTICA:</strong> Towards an Accessibility-Based Framework for Assessing Freight Transport Poverty. Presented September 2026; accepted for future monograph publication.</li><li><strong>LSTP:</strong> Microsimulation-Based Assessment of the Impact of Passenger Traffic on the Reliability of Freight Transport under Urban Congestion Conditions. Presented September 2026; manuscript preparation ongoing.</li><li><strong>Elsevier chapter:</strong> Blockchain-Based Secure Communication in Digital Twins for Smart Transportation. Submitted July 2026; expected 2027, not yet published.</li></ul></section></div><p class="content-date">Updated {{ portfolio.updated }} · Full portfolio: <a href="https://ahmedalmadhoun.com/">ahmedalmadhoun.com</a><br>This is a concise professional profile. Research objectives and forthcoming outputs are labelled separately from completed publications.</p></main></body></html>
